---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

// Cite only sources that support their row; update the date and sources together.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const blob = 'https://github.com/lemun/kitzur/blob/main/';
const reviewed = 'October 27, 2026';
const nativeNote = 'Native client compaction (OpenCode): not compared yet (2026-10-27)';
const sources = [
	{ n: 1, href: `${blob}DESIGN.md`, text: 'Kitzur design (DESIGN.md)' },
	{ n: 2, href: `${blob}README.md#benchmarks`, text: 'Kitzur README: what is kept, summarized and lost' },
	{ n: 3, href: `${blob}CONFIG.md#client-setup-opencode-and-kilo`, text: 'Client setup: OpenCode and Kilo (CONFIG.md)' },
	{ n: 4, href: `${blob}bench/README.md#historical-gobstopper-comparison`, text: 'Historical Gobstopper comparison (bench/README.md)' },
	{ n: 5, href: `${blob}docs/GOBSTOPPER-INTEROP.md`, text: 'Gobstopper legacy stats interop (docs/GOBSTOPPER-INTEROP.md)' },
	{ n: 6, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/blob/1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939/docs/proxy.md', text: 'Gobstopper proxy documentation (snapshot 1aa7129)' },
	{ n: 7, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/blob/1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939/docs/context-retention.md', text: 'Gobstopper context retention (snapshot 1aa7129)' },
	{ n: 8, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/blob/1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939/README.md', text: 'Gobstopper README (snapshot 1aa7129)' },
	{ n: 9, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/blob/1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939/docs/session-data.md', text: 'Gobstopper session data (snapshot 1aa7129)' },
	{ n: 10, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/blob/1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md', text: 'Gobstopper third-party notices (snapshot 1aa7129)' },
	{ n: 11, href: 'https://github.com/hraness/gobstopper/releases/tag/v0.8.5', text: 'Gobstopper v0.8.5 release' },
];
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Compare',
		description:
			'How Kitzur behaves next to an agent’s own compaction and Gobstopper, dimension by dimension, with sources.',
	}}
>
	<p>
		<strong>Reviewed {reviewed}.</strong> This compares behaviour, not quality. {nativeNote}
		Checked 2026-10-19 against Gobstopper v0.8.10 commit 1aa71294f35d07ff81c82a7e133d0c2a3a220939.
		Kitzur was inspired by Gobstopper.
	</p>

	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Dimension</th>
				<th>Kitzur</th>
				<th>Native client compaction (OpenCode)</th>
				<th>Gobstopper v0.8.10 (snapshot 2026-10-19)</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Where it runs</th>
				<td>Loopback proxy between the agent and its model server <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Loopback proxy between agent and provider <sup>[6]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Who writes the summary</th>
				<td>Deterministic extraction. No model is called <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>One mechanical summary of older turns; no model call <sup>[6][10]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">When it compacts</th>
				<td>When a request would exceed the prompt budget for the served window, below the client’s own compaction point <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>When request passes <code>--threshold</code> (default 128,000 tokens; README benchmark used 45,000); v0.8.5 clipped per-scope thresholds to input capacity <sup>[6][8][11]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">What stays word for word</th>
				<td>System prompts, tool definitions and recent messages, with tool calls kept next to their results <sup>[1][2]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Head plus last three turns; optional <code>--keep-tail-percent</code> retains older whole turns (default 0) <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Large tool output</th>
				<td>Old snapshots become stubs; other oversized results keep a head and tail <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Older results may be head/tail excerpts with omitted count and SHA-256; defaults are 2,000 chars per result and 32,000 chars/262,144 bytes total (max 128) <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Repeated prefixes</th>
				<td>Forwarded messages stay unchanged between compactions under the default policy <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Bounded in-memory prefix cache; over-limit entry is rebuilt from client history <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Wire formats</th>
				<td>OpenAI Chat Completions only <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Anthropic Messages, OpenAI Responses and Chat Completions <sup>[6]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row"><code>qa46-ref</code> run (v0.7.2), 100k/32k: planted facts</th>
				<td>7/7 (Kitzur predecessor, defaults) <sup>[4]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>4/7 (tuned) <sup>[4]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Same run: prompt tokens, all attempts</th>
				<td>1,710,746 <sup>[4]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>1,734,118 <sup>[4]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Client-removed history</th>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Cannot recover history removed by client; cache rebuilds on next request; no automatic durable store for Chat Completions proxy clients <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Stats</th>
				<td>JSONL stats that a Gobstopper release with <code>data import-legacy</code> can import as estimates <sup>[5]</sup></td>
				<td>Not compared</td>
				<td>Legacy proxy-stats JSONL import estimates sizes; no request IDs, tokens or speed <sup>[9]</sup></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="reading">Reading the table</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Kitzur does not replace native compaction. Kitzur’s client setup keeps the agent’s own compaction
			on as a fallback <sup>[3]</sup>.
		</li>
		<li>
			The historical v0.7.2 rows are simulated sessions against a mock server, measured before scenario
			sanitation. They are not a test of current Gobstopper or of real-model quality, and are not
			comparable with the <a href={`${base}/benchmarks/`}>current benchmark figures</a> <sup>[4]</sup>.
		</li>
		<li>Fact counts show whether planted markers survive, not whether a model understands them.</li>
		<li>Gobstopper’s own Terminal-Bench 2.1 result for v0.7.2, as its README reports it (89 tasks, one trial per arm): 61 tasks solved with Gobstopper vs 60 without, and 84.3M input tokens with Gobstopper vs 118.6M without; these are volumes, not costs. Kitzur has no Terminal-Bench run, so this is not a comparison with Kitzur <sup>[8]</sup>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
	<ol>
		{sources.map((s) => <li id={`source-${s.n}`}><a href={s.href}>{s.text}</a></li>)}
	</ol>
</StarlightPage>
